{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What is the main purpose of underwater cables? Why are cables laid on the seabed?", "output": "Submarine cables are transmission links used for transmitting power and communication signals across sea areas. Their main uses are to support undersea oil and gas extraction, marine scientific research, utilization of undersea energy, transportation, and undersea culture and tourism, among others. Due to the good insulation and transmission performance of seawater, laying cables underwater has advantages such as stability, efficiency, and safety, and it can also avoid large-scale occupation of land resources and damage to the environment."}{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What is the main purpose of the warships in the East China Sea?", "output": "The warships in the East Sea are primarily used for maritime military operations and safeguarding national maritime interests. They hold responsibilities such as protecting maritime safety, upholding territorial sovereignty, executing maritime patrols, and combating piracy. The presence and activities of these warships play a crucial role in maintaining regional security and stability."}
